a local mother is speaking out after a  confrontation between  school staff and her 13 year old son  with autism over him  not wearing a mask chantelle myers is  hoping to raise some awareness about how  to engage with students with special  needs and  how to prevent a situation like this  from happening to other families  kate houston reports typical teenage boy  loves baseball  bacon cars water swimming  and he has autism chantal myers is the  mother to 13-year-old christian myers  who has autism  myers says the past year of distance  learning has been tough  he hasn't had any social interaction  hasn't been around a lot of typical  peers which  you know obviously he's regressed in the  last year  substantially this week all grades were  able to return to school on a hybrid  model  myers took these photos of christian as  he entered the school for the first time  in over a year then all of a sudden i  just hear somebody  yelling from around the corner mask mask  where is his mask he needs a mask  and i looked at christian because i was  like well  what's going on here he wasn't wearing a  mask christian won't wear a mask because  of sensory issues  the organization for autism research  says mask wearing has been a challenge  for people with autism throughout the  pandemic  and has led to other confrontations  initially myers was told by the school  she needed a doctor's note in order for  christian to be in class without a mask  later they clarified she would need to  modify his individualized education  program  i'm surprised that he handled it as well  as he did because  not coming back into the building you  know or not being there for a year  and then being hit with that aggressive  attitude  or you know it was just uncalled for and  unprofessional i think in response ccsd  referred channel 8 to the hybrid model  guide which says  in part that a student with a disability  that prevents them from wearing a mask  may qualify for accommodations but it  must be documented in the student's iep  if anybody's at home because their kiddo  you know has to wear a mask to school  there's options and i just would hate  for somebody to experience what we did  yesterday and  it could have been handled completely  different kate houston 8 news now  myers has scheduled an iep revision with  the school next week to allow  christian to not wear a mask in the  meantime he will head back to class  on monday with his cohort denise
 

